    "--- \n",
    "## 2. Time Complexity: Lookup & Access ($O(1)$ vs $O(n)$)\n",
    "\n",
    "Understanding the underlying data structure is critical for writing efficient algorithms. Searching for an item in a `list` requires scanning elements sequentially ($O(n)$), whereas set and dictionary lookups rely on hashing algorithms for instantaneous ($O(1)$ average case) retrieval."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": None,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "N = 5_000_000\n",
    "large_list = list(range(N))\n",
    "large_set = set(large_list)\n",
    "target_val = N - 1  # Worst-case item (at the end)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. List Membership Lookup (O(n))\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "found_in_list = target_val in large_list\n",
    "t_list = time.time() - t0\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Set Membership Lookup (O(1))\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "found_in_set = target_val in large_set\n",
    "t_set = time.time() - t0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"List Lookup Time (O(n)): {t_list:.6f} seconds\")\n",
    "print(f\"Set Lookup Time (O(1)):  {t_set:.6f} seconds\")\n",
    "print(f\"⚡ Set is ~{t_list / max(t_set, 1e-9):.1f}x faster for target lookup!\")"
   ]
