    "--- \n",
    "## 4. Shallow Copy vs. Deep Copy\n",
    "\n",
    "When copying nested data structures, understanding reference copying is essential to avoid unexpected side effects:\n",
    "- **Shallow Copy (`copy.copy`):** Creates a new container object, but populates it with references to the child objects contained in the original.\n",
    "- **Deep Copy (`copy.deepcopy`):** Recursively creates brand new copies of both the parent container and all nested child objects."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": None,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import copy\n",
    "\n",
    "original_nested = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Shallow Copy\n",
    "shallow_copied = copy.copy(original_nested)\n",
    "# 2. Deep Copy\n",
    "deep_copied = copy.deepcopy(original_nested)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mutate nested element\n",
    "original_nested[0][0] = 999\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Original:\", original_nested)\n",
    "print(\"Shallow Copy (Affected!):\", shallow_copied)\n",
    "print(\"Deep Copy (Isolated!):\", deep_copied)"
   ]
